🚀 Day 2 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 540 – Single Element in a Sorted Array.

This problem deepened my understanding of Binary Search and how the properties of sorted arrays can be used to find the unique element in O(log n) time with O(1) extra space.

💡 Approach: Modified Binary Search (Parity-Based)

Instead of checking every element, I used Binary Search along with the observation that duplicate elements appear in pairs. By analyzing whether the mid index is even or odd and comparing it with its neighboring element, I determined which half of the array contained the single element. This allowed me to eliminate half of the search space in every iteration.

📚 Key Learnings:
✅ Applying Binary Search on paired elements
✅ Using index parity (even/odd) to optimize the search
✅ Identifying patterns in sorted arrays
✅ Reducing the search space efficiently in every iteration
✅ Achieving an optimized O(log n) solution with O(1) space

